w: 1.~Praise waits in Zi- on, _ Lord, for Thee; There _ we will _ pay our vow; O Thou, the God that hea- rest _ prayer, Be- fore Thee _ all shall bow.
w: 2.~A- gainst me my be- _ set- ting sins Pre- _ vail from _ day to day, But Thou in Thy for- giv- ing _ grace Wilt take them _ all a- way.
w: 3.~O blest the man whom _ Thou dost choose, And _ draw in _ love to Thee, That in Thy sac- red courts, O _ Lord, He may a _ dwel- ler be.
w: 4.~We sure- ly shall be _ sa- tis- fied With _ Thy a- _ bun- dant grace, Yea, with the good- ness of Thy _ house, Of Thy most _ ho- ly place.
